{
  "about": "Send feedback: what every app sends to the issues relay, and what each answer means. A draft (kind, message, optional email, source, the sheet's clientID) plus coarse facts about the device become the request body; never anything from the tasks. The message: control characters removed (except new lines and tabs), trimmed, cut to maxMessage code points (2000 unless the case says), trimmed again; nothing left means nothing to send (body null). The title is \"<Kind> · <Platform>: <message>\" in full (the relay shortens it). The email is trimmed and left out when empty. Metadata keeps this key order and leaves out what isn't known. Answers: 2xx is sent; 408, 429, 5xx and no answer at all (offline, status null) mean try again with the same clientID; any other 4xx failed. Checked by the C# core (FeedbackFixtureTests), the server (FeedbackApiTests), the web app (feedback.test.mjs), Swift (FeedbackTests) and Kotlin (FeedbackTest).",
